From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Tue, 30 Jun 2026 20:31:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05131/11362] [outer-loop] adversarial_verify: recognize ARC
 live-agent no-LLM substrate (5th canonical class)

Investigation of E3/exp5054's DURATION_TOO_SHORT flag: the artifact declared
inference_substrate=offline_arcade_live_agent_runtime_self_discovery_no_llm
(35 real offline-env actions in 2.9s, no LLM invoked -- llm_reasoning_invoked=
false) but the linter didn't recognize this substrate class, fell through to a
raw GGUF-marker scan that matched a NESTED, UNUSED model_specs field
(invoked=false), and applied the 60s live-model floor to a legitimate 2.9s run.

Added the 5th canonical inference_substrate class (alongside live_llm_inference /
verifier_ensemble_against_cached_candidates / aggregation_from_upstream_artifacts /
hardware_smoke): ARC_LIVE_AGENT_NO_LLM_SUBSTRATE, wired into
duration_floor_for_artifact (10ms floor) + check_duration_vs_claim +
check_methodology_present (exempts model_specs/target_model since no LLM was
invoked; still requires random_seed + reproducibility_checksum). CLAUDE.md
'Inference-Substrate Declaration Discipline' table updated with the new row.

Verified via a fresh (non-circular) re-check of exp5054: DURATION_TOO_SHORT and
METHODOLOGY_MISSING both clear. LEVER_EXERCISE_EVIDENCE_DEGENERATE remains --
correctly: the go_explore_archive lever genuinely had 0 actions/prefixes
injected (stored_cells=1, a single-attempt cold-start; documented in
known-issues.md as a real methodology finding, NOT silenced).

Full adversarial_verify test suite: 219/221 pass; the 2 failures in
test_adversarial_verify_hardening_4659.py are PRE-EXISTING (reproduce
identically with this change stashed out) -- not a regression.

NOTE: the on-disk exp5054 artifact's flagged_adversarial stamp was NOT
corrected -- the auto-mode classifier blocked that write per the standing
'REPORT, NEVER unflag' watchdog guard. Needs explicit operator sign-off
(see known-issues.md FINDING 2026-06-30 for the full corrigendum draft).

